    "body": "## Motivation\n\nClosing the fastsafetensors loader alone leaves its returned file buffer allocated after each shard.\n\n## Change\n\nClose the buffer before the loader. Tests cover normal loading, early iterator close, and read and cleanup errors.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe targeted suite passes: 24 tests and 2 subtests. On one GB10, the 52-shard NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4 model loaded and served. Reported warm-cache weight-load memory fell from 47.12 GB to 27.03 GB; load time was 12.67 s versus 12.42 s. This is not a throughput or accuracy benchmark.\n\nThe cached image used sglang-kernel 0.4.6.post1 rather than the 0.4.7 required by current main, so its version check was bypassed for the model run. The unit tests were rerun on current main. This change does not address the separate multi-node device-index issue in #29272.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35302733744](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35302733744)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35302733577](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35302733577)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35302733799](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35302733799)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
